 "saas:SUP-7768": {
  "key": "SUP-7768",
  "requestType": "API",
  "summary": "429 errors during month-end invoice upload",
  "resolution": "Retry storm on Growth plan; customer moved to /v2/invoices/batch and honored Retry-After.",
  "kbUsed": [
   "KB-8"
  ],
  "customer": {
   "opening": "During month-end our invoice upload job gets lots of \"429 Too Many Requests\" and fails halfway through. We need a higher limit urgently, close is in 2 days.",
   "persona": "Busy finance/engineering-side customer under deadline pressure (month-end close in 2 days). Tone is urgent but polite. Tech level is moderate: knows their job fires about 50 requests per second and can guess at causes like Retry-After handling, but isn't an API expert. Writes short, plain, casual messages of one or two sentences. Candid about possible fault ('Honestly I think we...'). Gives answers only when asked and doesn't volunteer extra detail. Patience is fairly high as long as a fix is quick, and is happy once it works.",
   "facts": [
    {
     "id": "h1",
     "detail": "It fires roughly 50 requests per second, one invoice per call.",
     "asked_by": "Asks about the job's request rate, volume, or how it sends invoices (per-call or batched).",
     "kind": "fact"
    },
    {
     "id": "h2",
     "detail": "We're on the Growth plan.",
     "asked_by": "Asks which plan, tier, or account level they are on.",
     "kind": "fact"
    },
    {
     "id": "h3",
     "detail": "Honestly I think we ignore the Retry-After header, it just retries immediately.",
     "asked_by": "Asks how the client handles 429 responses, retries, backoff, or the Retry-After header.",
     "kind": "fact"
    },
    {
     "id": "h4",
     "detail": "Switched to batch with backoff and the run finished in 6 minutes with zero 429s. Great.",
     "asked_by": "Agent suggests using batch requests and exponential backoff or honoring Retry-After, and the customer reports the result after trying it.",
     "kind": "reaction"
    }
   ],
   "secret": [
    "Rate-limit",
    "v2/invoices/batch"
   ]
  },
  "debrief": [
   {
    "from": "customer",
    "author": "Avery Haddad",
    "public": true,
    "body": "During month-end our invoice upload job gets lots of \"429 Too Many Requests\" and fails halfway through. We need a higher limit urgently, close is in 2 days."
   },
   {
    "from": "agent",
    "author": "Sofia",
    "public": true,
    "body": "Hi Avery, let's get your close through. How many requests per second does the job send at peak? Which Ledgerline plan are you on? And when it gets a 429, does your client wait for the Retry-After header before retrying? Sofia"
   },
   {
    "from": "customer",
    "author": "Avery Haddad",
    "public": true,
    "body": "It fires roughly 50 requests per second, one invoice per call. We're on the Growth plan. Honestly I think we ignore the Retry-After header, it just retries immediately."
   },
   {
    "from": "agent",
    "author": "Sofia",
    "public": false,
    "body": "Rate-limit metrics: tenant peak 312 rps from immediate retries (retry storm). Growth = 20 rps. Recommend batch endpoint /v2/invoices/batch + honoring Retry-After."
   },
   {
    "from": "agent",
    "author": "Sofia",
    "public": true,
    "body": "Thanks Avery. The Growth plan allows 20 requests per second, and immediate retries multiply the traffic, which keeps the job throttled. Two changes should fix it: send invoices through /v2/invoices/batch, which takes up to 100 invoices per call and counts as one request, and wait the number of seconds in Retry-After before any retry. That brings you well under the limit. A higher permanent limit would need a plan change; I can put you in touch with your account manager if you'd like to discuss. Sofia"
   },
   {
    "from": "customer",
    "author": "Avery Haddad",
    "public": true,
    "body": "Switched to batch with backoff and the run finished in 6 minutes with zero 429s. Great."
   }
  ],
  "value": {
   "score": 100,
   "usable": true,
   "sensitive": false,
   "reasons": [
    "3 customer messages",
    "clear resolution",
    "linked KB article",
    "has internal notes for the debrief"
   ]
  }
 },
